    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23329" root="شوف" body-key="$">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشاف عَلَيْهِ</span></b>  <i>i. q.</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْرَفَ</span> [meaning <i>He was,</i> or
<i>became, on the brink,</i> or <i>verge,</i> or <i>at the point, of
it</i>], (S, O, K,) namely, a thing; like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَشْفَى</span>; (S,
O;) from which it is formed by transposition.
(S.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشاف</span> <i>He feared.</i> (Ibn-'Abbád, O,
K.) You say, <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اشاف مِنْهُ</span> <i>He feared him,</i> or <i>it.</i>
(K.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also 5, last sentence.

